From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Tree impostors

Shape.impostor: instances drawn as quads showing the three captured
views (8 x 8 hemi-octahedral atlas) nearest the camera's direction,
lit from captured mean normals, with per-texel depth for the depth
buffer and shadows. Quads sit at the front of their capture sphere, so
texel depths only push fragments back, declared with depth_greater:
the GPU rejects hidden fragments before shading.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0017-impostors: backdrop 59 -> 20 ms per step; impostors within 4% of
  full trees
- 0023-impostor-early-depth: impostors 7.1 -> 4.2 ms
